sequenceDiagram
  participant R as Receptionist R1
  participant Dr as Dr. Example One
  participant Web as Web app
  participant API
  participant Q as QueueOrchestrator
  participant Pay as PaymentsService
  participant PG as PostgreSQL
  R->>Web: Create Sample Patient A
  Web->>API: POST /patients
  API->>PG: patient with next P- number, audit row
  R->>Web: Book appointment
  Web->>API: POST /appointments
  API->>PG: appointment scheduled, database blocks doctor overlap
  R->>Web: Check in and get token
  Web->>API: PATCH /appointments/:id/check-in
  API->>Q: checkInAppointment
  Q->>PG: session, token, queue entry waiting, appointment checked_in
  Dr->>Web: Call next, then Patient is here start
  Web->>API: PATCH /queue/entries/:id/start-consultation
  Q->>PG: entry in_consultation, encounter created
  Dr->>Web: Notes, treatments done, Sign and print prescription
  Web->>API: POST /encounters/:id/treatments, POST /prescriptions, POST /prescriptions/:id/finalize
  Dr->>Web: Complete visit
  Web->>API: PATCH /queue/entries/:id/complete
  Q->>PG: entry and appointment completed, consultation and treatment charges with commission snapshot
  R->>Web: Billing desk, Bill, Receive
  Web->>API: POST /payments
  API->>Pay: collect
  Pay->>PG: one transaction - invoice INV, receipt REC, allocations, commission entries, ledger
  API-->>Web: receipt and invoice numbers
  R->>Web: Print receipt and invoice
